@startuml atsecure
'
' Engineered by  Christian Schnapka
'                Embedded Principal+ Engineer
'                Macstab GmbH · Hamburg, Germany
'                https://macstab.com
'
' AT_SECURE at execve: when the kernel sets it, what the loader then does
' with LD_PRELOAD, and what a libchaos constructor does when it is loaded.
'
' Reference: docs/SAFETY.md §1, docs/PLATFORM.md §6
'            ld.so(8) "Secure-execution mode", getauxval(3)
'            Linux kernel fs/exec.c, security/commoncap.c
'
title AT_SECURE Auxv Flag — Privilege Strip for LD_PRELOAD

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 4
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor                 #2C3E50
  LifeLineBorderColor        #2C3E50
  LifeLineBackgroundColor    #ECF0F1
  ParticipantBorderColor     #2C3E50
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontStyle       bold
  GroupBackgroundColor       #FDFEFE
  GroupBorderColor           #95A5A6
}
hide footbox

participant "execve() caller\n(user process)" as Caller
participant "Linux kernel\nfs/exec.c"          as Kernel
participant "ld.so\n(dynamic linker)"          as Ldso
participant "libchaos-<lib>.so\n(LD_PRELOAD)"  as Chaos
participant "libc"                             as Libc

Caller -> Kernel : execve("/path/to/target", argv, envp)
note right of Caller
  envp contains LD_PRELOAD=/path/libchaos-io-glibc-amd64.so
end note

Kernel -> Kernel : load ELF, compute new credentials
note right of Kernel
  AT_SECURE = 1 if the exec changes
  euid/egid (setuid/setgid bit), raises
  permitted capabilities (file caps),
  or an LSM requests it; else 0.
  no_new_privs: setuid bits and file
  caps are ignored → no change → 0.
end note

Kernel -> Ldso : enter PT_INTERP with auxv on the stack

alt AT_SECURE == 1
  Ldso -> Ldso : glibc: drop LD_PRELOAD entries containing '/'\nmusl: ignore LD_PRELOAD entirely
  note right of Ldso
    libchaos-<lib>.so is never mapped.
    glibc also removes the unsecure variables
    (LD_PRELOAD, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, ...)
    from the program's environment.
  end note
  Ldso -> Libc : map DT_NEEDED, relocate, run initialisers
  Ldso -> Caller : _start: no interposition
else AT_SECURE == 0
  Ldso -> Chaos : map each LD_PRELOAD object (after the executable)
  Ldso -> Libc : map DT_NEEDED objects
  Ldso -> Ldso : relocate; references to interposed names\nbind to the first definition: libchaos
  Ldso -> Libc : run initialisers, dependencies first
  Ldso -> Chaos : libchaos constructor
  note right of Chaos
    1. ensure_symbols(): dlsym(RTLD_NEXT)
       for the whole table, once (chaos_once)
    2. seed the process PRNG
    3. config_init(): empty snapshots,
       stamp UNKNOWN
    4. config_prepare(): load the rule file,
       write the status file
  end note
  Ldso -> Caller : _start / main with interposition active
end

note across
  Check a running target: grep libchaos /proc/<pid>/maps
  Check from inside a program: getauxval(AT_SECURE) != 0 means secure-execution mode.
  A helper such as printenv proves nothing: it is not privileged and does load the library.
end note

@enduml
